# Implementation Plan: PWA Web Push Notifications

Enable native lockscreen push notifications for mobile PWA users when the app is closed, triggered whenever a doctor or admin updates an appointment.

## Architecture & Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant MobilePWA as Mobile PWA / Service Worker
    participant AngularApp as Angular Frontend
    participant Backend as C# ASP.NET Core Backend
    participant WebPushServer as Web Push Service (FCM/Mozilla/Apple)

    AngularApp->>MobilePWA: Request Notification Permission
    MobilePWA-->>AngularApp: Granted & Device Push Subscription Token
    AngularApp->>Backend: POST /api/notifications/subscribe-push (Device Token & VAPID keys)
    Backend->>Backend: Store User Push Subscription in DB

    Note over Backend: Doctor completes / confirms appointment
    Backend->>WebPushServer: Send Encrypted Web Push Payload (VAPID Signed)
    WebPushServer->>MobilePWA: Deliver Push Event to Service Worker (App Closed)
    MobilePWA->>MobilePWA: Display Native OS Lockscreen Alert ("HealSync Appointment Update")
```

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Web Push Notifications require user permission on their mobile browser (*"Allow HealSync to send notifications"*). Once allowed, notifications are delivered directly to their phone lockscreen even when the browser or app tab is closed.

